stateDiagram-v2
  state "Choosing a sign-in method" as s0
  state "Told a connection is needed" as s1
  state "At Google or Apple" as s2
  state "Confirming a matching account" as s3
  state "Told matching proof expired" as s4
  state "Told provider sign-in failed" as s5
  state "Told account proof does not match" as s6
  state "Signed in to the chosen account" as s7
  state "Guest profile kept" as s8
  state "Choosing sign-in methods to connect" as s9
  state "Told the method cannot be connected" as s10
  state "Confirming method removal" as s11
  state "Told the last method must remain" as s12
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s2: Chooses an available provider online
  s0 --> s1: Chooses a provider offline
  s1 --> s0: Connection returns
  s2 --> s7: Provider identifies an existing account
  s2 --> s7: Provider identifies a new verified address match without an Apple relay
  s2 --> s3: Provider identifies an address match needing account proof
  s2 --> s7: Provider identifies a new account without a match
  s2 --> s5: Provider has trouble
  s2 --> s8: Abandons provider sign-in
  s3 --> s7: Proves the matching account
  s3 --> s7: Keeps the accounts separate
  s3 --> s6: Proves a different account
  s3 --> s4: The ten-minute chance to confirm expires
  s4 --> s0: Starts sign-in again
  s5 --> s2: Tries provider sign-in again
  s6 --> s3: Tries proving the matching account again
  s7 --> s9: Opens connected sign-in methods
  s7 --> s0: The thirty-day sign-in expires
  s7 --> s0: SignedOut
  s8 --> s0: Starts signing in again
  s9 --> s7: Connects an available method of a different provider
  s9 --> s10: Connects a method already owned elsewhere or of the same provider
  s9 --> s11: Removes a method while another remains
  s9 --> s12: Removes the only method
  s10 --> s9: Returns to connected methods
  s11 --> s9: Confirms removal
  s12 --> s9: Returns to connected methods
